zl-agent (1.0.6-1) stable; urgency=medium

  * Offer a model picker on first launch when more than one model is pulled.
    The choice is remembered; "/models" changes it later.
  * Align the dark colour scheme with the ZealLab palette. Warning, error and
    success indicators, and diff colours, are unchanged.

 -- ZealLab LLC <info@zeallab.com>  Sun, 23 Aug 2026 18:16:12 -0400

zl-agent (1.0.4-1) stable; urgency=medium

  * Fix an empty model list when OLLAMA_HOST has no port. OLLAMA_HOST=0.0.0.0
    is the usual way to expose Ollama on the LAN; the agent resolved that to
    port 80 and found nothing, so no models appeared even though the daemon
    was running.
  * Make the local-only defaults apply in the shipped binary. They were set by
    mutating the environment at startup, which bundling defeated, so the agent
    could contact models.dev and load a cloud provider catalogue.
  * Ignore a stale models.dev cache left in ~/.cache/opencode by earlier
    versions; delete it to reclaim ~4 MB.
  * Retire "/connect" and remove cloud-provider wording from the interface.

 -- ZealLab LLC <info@zeallab.com>  Sun, 23 Aug 2026 17:20:47 -0400

zl-agent (1.0.1-1) stable; urgency=medium

  * Prompt edge, its bottom stub and the spinner now use the ZealLab brand
    blue instead of the rotating per-agent colour.
  * Logo background squares tint toward main_blue rather than the text
    colour.
  * "/connect" lists the models the local Ollama daemon actually has,
    instead of opening the cloud provider authentication dialog.
  * The models.dev cloud provider catalog is no longer compiled into the
    binary, so no cloud providers can be offered.

 -- ZealLab LLC <info@zeallab.com>  Sun, 23 Aug 2026 00:34:15 -0400

zl-agent (1.0.0-1) stable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release. Adds the "zl agent" subcommand: a local AI coding
    agent backed by Ollama.

 -- ZealLab LLC <info@zeallab.com>  Sat, 22 Aug 2026 22:00:00 -0400
